-- A REFUSE message is a LITERAL, not an expression: the grammar admits only a
-- literal in that position, so a computed message is a PARSE error rather than
-- a type error.
--
-- That is deliberate. A refusal's reason is readable without running the
-- program, so it can be reported, and read per reason, from the source alone;
-- and a literal payload is what lets the evaluation machine raise a refusal
-- with no new stack frame.

GIVETH A NUMBER
`bad refusal` MEANS REFUSE (1 PLUS 1)
